4. EDITIONS AND LICENSE KEY

Cascera can be installed and used free of charge. Features marked Premium in
the Software, as the edition table in Help > License shows, require a
Premium license key; Premium is likewise licensed for personal,
non-commercial use. A 14-day trial is available once per computer.

A Premium license key is personal to one person:

  - A key may be used on up to 3 computers at the same time. You can
    release a computer in Arctisoft Studio Hub to use the license on
    another one. A computer that has not used the license for 45 days is
    released automatically.
  - Sharing, publishing or distributing your license key is prohibited.
  - A license may be passed on only as a whole, using the transfer
    function in Arctisoft Studio Hub. After a transfer you may no longer
    use it.
  - Keys that are misused or obtained by fraud may be deactivated.

A Premium license covers the major version it was sold for and every
update within it.

The computers using a license are recorded solely to apply these limits,
not to track individual user activity.

5. DATA PROCESSING AND PRIVACY

Controller: Arctisoft Studio / Bernd Julian Hagen, Austria,
support@arctisoft-studio.com. The Privacy Policy at
https://arctisoft-studio.com/legal/privacy explains your rights under the
GDPR, retention periods and how to complain to a supervisory authority.

Account and license (when you sign in through Arctisoft Studio Hub):

  - Your account email, your license records and, if you upload one in
    Arctisoft Studio Hub, your profile image.
  - For each computer that uses a license or starts a trial: its name, a
    one-way digest of the Windows installation's identifier, a one-way
    digest of the hardware identifier its firmware reports, and the IP
    address at registration. They apply the limit of three computers and
    one trial per computer (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR).

Preference and history sync (optional):

An Arctisoft account is optional for Cascera. When signed in, you can store
the Cascera preferences you choose and, if history tracking is on, recent
download history with your account (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). History records
can include addresses, titles, dates, outcomes, formats, output file paths
and measured media properties; output paths may contain personal folder
names. Cloud history keeps a bounded set of recent records; device history
and exported records are separate from it. Settings > Privacy & Sync
controls both; history offers removal, clearing and export.

Connected features (only when you use them):

  - Downloads: the address you enter, and the requests yt-dlp makes to
    that website on your behalf, go to the website you download from. That
    website's own terms and privacy policy apply.
  - Media tools: yt-dlp and FFmpeg are downloaded from their publishers on
    GitHub when missing or outdated. Media discovery opens pages in the
    Microsoft Edge installed on your computer, without your Edge profile.
  - Browser cookies: only when you choose a browser for cookies in
    Settings, yt-dlp reads that browser's cookies on your computer and
    sends them only to the website you download from.

Software updates:

The Software can check Arctisoft Studio's public release feed on GitHub
for updates. These requests carry normal network information and the
application's version, never your files.

Workspace state, queues, device statistics and device history are stored
on your computer. Downloaded media, file contents, browser passwords and
activity outside Cascera are never uploaded. The Software has no analytics
or telemetry. Cloud data and your account can be deleted in Arctisoft
Studio Hub (Account & Security) or by contacting support. Uninstalling the
Software keeps your files and local application data and does not delete
your Arctisoft account.

