THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt in the installation folder lists every component
with its version, license, copyright notice and project address; the
license texts are installed with it. The installer uses the Inter and
Cormorant Garamond typefaces under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Nothing
in this agreement limits the rights those licenses grant for their
components.

TagLib# is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1. It is
a separate library that Cascera loads at run time; you may replace it with a
modified version, and its source code is available as
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt describes.

yt-dlp (The Unlicense) and FFmpeg (a GPL build) are downloaded on your
computer from their publishers and are licensed to you by them, not by
Arctisoft Studio.

